From: Benjamin Larsson <banan@ludd.ltu.se>
Subject: [PATCH] usb-storage: ignore the OTi-2208 USB host-to-host cable

The OTi-2208 "EasySuite USB Host-to-Host Data Bridge" (0ea0:2108) presents
each cable end as a Bulk-Only mass-storage device with a single CD-ROM LUN
that holds the vendor's Windows software. The data link itself is driven by
vendor SCSI commands over the same interface and is handled by the
oti2208_net network driver, which speaks Bulk-Only Transport itself.

Let usb-storage ignore the device so oti2208_net can bind to it. The entry
is limited to bcdDevice 0x0100, the revision of the 2208 cables tested;
older OTi-2108 cables share the USB ID.

Signed-off-by: Benjamin Larsson <banan@ludd.ltu.se>
---
 drivers/usb/storage/unusual_devs.h | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/storage/unusual_devs.h b/drivers/usb/storage/unusual_devs.h
--- a/drivers/usb/storage/unusual_devs.h
+++ b/drivers/usb/storage/unusual_devs.h
@@ -1618,6 +1618,17 @@
 		US_FL_FIX_INQUIRY ),
 
 /*
+ * OTi-2208 USB host-to-host cable ("EasySuite USB Host-to-Host Data Bridge").
+ * Each end shows up as a CD-ROM holding the Windows software; the data link
+ * itself is driven by vendor SCSI commands and handled by oti2208_net.
+ */
+UNUSUAL_DEV(0x0ea0, 0x2108, 0x0100, 0x0100,
+		"OTi",
+		"OTi-2208 Data Bridge",
+		USB_SC_DEVICE, USB_PR_DEVICE, NULL,
+		US_FL_IGNORE_DEVICE),
+
+/*
  * Submitted by Daniel Drake <dsd@gentoo.org>
  * Reported by dayul on the Gentoo Forums
  */
